  "description": "Host-neutral engine behind the Shiny gauge controls — value-to-angle scale mapping for any start angle and sweep, nice-number tick generation, a fit-to-box layout that sizes semicircle and three-quarter dials to the space they are given, and the spring/ease needle physics (momentum carried through retargets, overshoot, stop pegs and the startup sweep) that make a speedometer or tachometer needle move like a real one. Used by the .NET MAUI and Blazor controls.",
